				{
					"id": "tr03rkGdRCt821j2O",
					"name": "Crush",
					"local_notes": "Lore: An invisible telekinetic grip that closes on a target's throat or chest, ignoring armour and impossible to dodge.\n\nDesign: Innate Attack (Crushing, 5/die) with Malediction (+100%, B36) and Armor Divisor (2) (+50%, B103), plus Warp Sorcery/Perils, net +120%. Full modified cost: 5 x 2.2 = 11 points/level. Bought at 8 levels (8d(2) cr, Malediction) for 88 points, the default a trained battlefield psyker buys (a lesser psyker may buy fewer). Needs Warp Empowerment level 8 (cap 90) at 8 levels.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mFjYw6c-SUD-ytpdT",
							"name": "Malediction 1",
							"cost_adj": "+100%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mOV_D1nvN2S-VJsb3",
							"name": "Armor Divisor (2)",
							"cost_adj": "+50%"
						},
						{
							"id": "m7zJX8fWz2T5HV0fZ",
							"name": "Warp Sorcery",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mzel64o2iNbZ453ga",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp",
							"cost_adj": "-10%"
						}
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 8
				},
				{
					"id": "tA-smJrMuhZZXT4Pg",
					"name": "Gate of Infinity",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Tears a hole between two points in real space and steps through — the rarest and most feared telekinetic feat, since a botched Gate can open into the warp itself instead.\n\nDesign: Built on Basic's own Warp advantage (B99, instant travel to any place you have seen/visualized, flat 100), with Preparation Required (-20%, B113, a few seconds' concentration) and the Severe Perils tier, reflecting the setting's specific fear of a failed Gate opening into the immaterium. Net -60%. Full modified cost: 100 x 0.4 = 40 points — the single most expensive non-Great-Power ability in this file; needs Warp Empowerment level 3 (cap 40), the minimum at which \"Delta and up\" can cast the full non-Great-Power roster, exactly on the cap with no headroom to spare.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mFOTAZTn1VLSKy6fh",
							"name": "Preparation Required",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mup-BAHqN509X3TVX",
							"name": "Warp Sorcery",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mnuW03io683O_svNR",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp (Severe)",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 100
				}
			]
		}
	],
	"skills": [
		{
			"id": "s23deCcqQeSKMci99",
			"name": "Psyniscience",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The trained (or instinctive) sense of \"something wrong\" in a presence, place, or object touched by the warp — a chill in a corridor, a servitor's dead eyes going wrong. Named for the Dark Heresy/Only War skill of the same purpose (Psyniscience), used here for calibration only; the GURPS build is original.\n\nDesign: New skill per framework.md (\"New skills only when nothing fits\"). Per/H with no default: nobody can roll it untrained. Characters with a Psyker Talent (see the psyker power library, not part of this file) get it at a discount per that trait's rules. An unaugmented human without any psychic Talent has nothing latent to sense with and must buy it as an unusual background purchase, if a GM allows it at all; most unaugmented Imperial citizens simply never take this skill.",
			"tags": [
				"Mental",
				"Imperium",
				"Psionic"
			],
			"difficulty": "per/h",
			"points": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "sWDd1JQa3ebA4hKvJ",
			"name": "Meditation",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The discipline every Librarian drills to hold their gift steady under fire.\n\nDesign: Meditation is Will/Hard (B207); 4 points = Will+0. The Battle-Brother base has Will 14 (IQ 11 from Personal Advancement, racial Will +2, Personal Advancement Will +1), so about 14.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Psyker"
			],
			"difficulty": "will/h",
			"points": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "s9nHN54DsHplKsDFq",
			"name": "Hidden Lore",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Librarian's formal training in the Chapter's Librarius doctrine on the immaterium.\n\nDesign: Average skill; points as above.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Psyker"
			],
			"specialization": "the Warp",
			"difficulty": "iq/a",
			"points": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "sV_jetDKpWXhdFBnr",
			"name": "Broadsword",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Many Librarians favour a force weapon over a chainsword once raised to the Librarius.\n\nDesign: Force swords use Broadsword (framework weapon-skill table), which the Battle-Brother template already has. These 4 points are added on top of it; merge the two Broadsword entries on the sheet.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Psyker"
			],
			"difficulty": "dx/a",
			"points": 4
		}
	],
	"equipment": [
		{
			"id": "ePTcO5t2g2v74E0Li",
			"description": "Force Sword, Astartes Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The blade of the Astartes Librarian: a Chapter-armoury power sword built to a Marine's grip and reach, with the psychic warding and focus crystals of a force weapon. Librarians of most Chapters favour a sword or staff, in Codex Space Marines background and Black Library Space Marine fiction.\n\nDesign: The human Force Sword's damage formula unchanged (sw+3d+1(10) field on, sw+1 field off), for the same reason the Astartes Power Sword is: \"sw\" resolves from the wielder's own ST, so a Marine (ST 30, sw 5d+2) rolls far more dice than a human without the weapon's line changing. Field-on is 8d+3(10), average 31, which penetrates Astartes plate always and Terminator plate (eff. DR 20) 98.6% of the time. Handling: the same heavier housing as the Astartes Power Sword: 9 lb and min ST 16, out of an unaugmented human's reach. Parry 0 (Broadsword). Cost $500 above the human pattern, as the Astartes Power Sword is above the human one.",
